 Project Structure

d:\Dynamic Task Manager\
├── index.html        Semantic HTML5 layout, accessible modals, stat cards & forms
├── style.css         Responsive styling, CSS variables, dark/light themes & animations
├── script.js         Vanilla JS application state, CRUD operations & event handling
└── README.md         Comprehensive documentation


 How to Run the Application

Because this is a pure front-end web application with no build steps or external dependencies, you can run it immediately:
 Option 1: Direct File Opening
1. Open the project folder `d:\Dynamic Task Manager\`.
2. Double-click index.html to open it in your default browser (Google Chrome, Microsoft Edge, Mozilla Firefox, Apple Safari, etc.).

 Option 2: Local HTTP Server (Optional)
If you prefer running through a local development server:

Using VS Code Live Server:
1. Open the folder in VS Code.
2. Right-click index.html and choose "Open with Live Server".


  Data Model & Schema
Each task object stored in the central tasks array adheres to the following structure:

typescript
interface Task {
  id: string;          // Unique string identifier (e.g. "task_...")
  title: string;       // Non-empty trimmed task title
  category: string;    // 'Work' | 'Personal' | 'Study' | 'Other'
  dueDate: string;     // ISO Date string 'YYYY-MM-DD' or ''
  completed: boolean;  // Boolean completion flag (false by default)
  createdAt: string;   // ISO 8601 Timestamp of creation
}
 Accessibility & Keyboard Shortcuts

- <kbd>Enter</kbd> inside form inputs: Submits the task creation or edit form.
- <kbd>Escape</kbd>: Immediately closes any open modal (Edit or Delete confirmation).
- <kbd>Tab</kbd> / <kbd>Shift+Tab</kbd>: Accessible sequential keyboard navigation across all buttons, inputs, checkboxes, and filters.
- Screen Reader Friendly**: Includes semantic HTML5 landmarks, ARIA labels (`aria-modal`, `role="dialog"`, `role="alert"`), and polite live regions.
